<!--
  What this application speaks, in the form xmpp.org reads.

  The list below was taken from the code rather than from memory: every entry
  corresponds either to a namespace this fork announces itself (see
  jabber_add_feature in Plugins/Purple Service/adiumPurpleJingle.m and
  adiumPurpleSignals.m) or to one the bundled libpurple announces on its behalf.

  Deliberately absent, because we do not do them: stream management (XEP-0198,
  the namespace exists in libpurple as a constant and is used nowhere), message
  archives (XEP-0313), message correction (XEP-0308) and direct TLS (XEP-0368).
  Claiming those would be worse than lacking them.

  OMEMO (XEP-0384) is listed as partial and means it: one to one conversations
  are encrypted and decrypted, and group chats are not. The older namespace
  eu.siacs.conversations.axolotl is the one spoken, which is what the clients
  on the other end speak.

  STILL TO DO before this is submitted anywhere: fill in <xmpp:version> per
  entry. Versions are left out rather than guessed, since naming the wrong
  revision of a specification is a worse answer than naming none.
-->
